s. The projective-deletion construction gives counterexamples over every finite field and makes the failure stronger than non-real roots alone.\n\nLimits: The manuscript is a first-version preprint and has not been conventionally peer reviewed. A specialist MathOverflow assessment reports that an independent counterexample was announced at ICM 2026 and verified, which supports the negative conclusion but does not review every argument in this paper.\n\nSources and record details\n\nStable ID: `math-matroid-kazhdan-lusztig-nonunimodal-2026` · Permanent record URL\n\n  * Primary Cheng and Liu, Kazhdan–Lusztig polynomials of matroids need not be unimodal\n  * Independent specialist assessment Luis Ferroni’s MathOverflow note on the paper and independently verified ICM counterexample\n\nAI involvement: The authors say the Rethlas agent, using GPT-5.6 Sol at max reasoning effort, found the motivating real-rootedness counterexample. The paper records the prompt, accepted output, discovery trajectory, human proofs and a repair after the agent’s verifier rejected an earlier step.\n\nChange history\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPosts (https://functor.network/entries)\nciteturn2search3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday;     * 24 Sep 2026 ... Fermat’s Last Theorem is formalized in Lean ... A proof of Sendov’s conjecture\n    * 9 Sep 2026\n\nFinite-time blowup for the 3D Navier–Stokes equations\n  *     * Bogdan Grechuk\n    * 7 Sep 2026\n\nTutte’s three-edge-colouring conjecture\n  *     * Bogdan Grechuk\n    * 6 Sep 2026\n\nTesting monotonicity of Boolean functions\n  *     * Bogdan Grechuk\n    * 5 Sep 2026\n\nLong gaps between primes\n  *     * Bogdan Grechuk\n    * 4 Sep 2026\n\nSmall gaps between primes\n\nPrice of Censorship in Multiple Concurrent Proposers under Sybils\n  *     * Bogdan Grechuk\n    * 3 Sep 2026\n\nThe Stanley–Stembridge conjecture is proved\n  *     * Bogdan Grechuk\n    * 2 Sep 2026\n\nSupercriti